  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Data analysis and probability on the EST II go beyond basic means and medians to include distributions, graphical representations, and counting methods.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Permutations",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( _nP_r=\\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Combinations",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\binom{n}{r}=\\dfrac{n!}{r!(n-r)!} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Conditional probability",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( P(A|B)=\\dfrac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Standard deviation",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "measures spread from mean",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "In how many ways can 3 students be chosen from a group of 8? \\[ \\binom{8}{3}=\\frac{8!}{3!\\cdot 5!}=\\frac{8\\times7\\times6}{6}=56. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Statistics, Counting & Probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Permutations (order matters): \\(^nP_r = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\). Combinations (order irrelevant): \\(^nC_r = \\dfrac{n!}{r!(n-r)!}\\). <strong>Conditional probability:</strong> \\(P(A|B) = \\dfrac{P(A \\cap B)}{P(B)}\\). Independent events: \\(P(A \\cap B) = P(A) \\cdot P(B)\\). Normal distribution: ~68% within \\(1\\sigma\\), ~95% within \\(2\\sigma\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Combinations with restrictions",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "From 4 boys and 5 girls, choose a team of 4 with at least 2 girls. How many ways? <p>Exactly 2G: \\(\\binom{5}{2}\\binom{4}{2}=10 \\times 6=60\\). Exactly 3G: \\(\\binom{5}{3}\\binom{4}{1}=10 \\times 4=40\\). Exactly 4G: \\(\\binom{5}{4}\\binom{4}{0}=5\\). Total: \\(105\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Events \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) are such that \\(P(A)=0.6\\), \\(P(B)=0.5\\), \\(P(A|B)=0.4\\). Find \\(P(A \\cup B)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(P(A \\cap B) = P(A|B)\\cdot P(B) = 0.4 \\times 0.5 = 0.2\\). \\(P(A \\cup B) = 0.6+0.5-0.2 = 0.9\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
